  <p>
    Solo travelling in Gokarna is common enough that nobody looks twice at a single backpacker
    checking into a hostel, sitting alone at a cafe table, or setting off on the beach trek without
    a group. It's one of the easier places in India to travel solo — small enough to navigate
    quickly, social enough that you're rarely alone unless you want to be.
  </p>

  <h2>Getting around solo</h2>
  <p>
    Gokarna town, Kudle Beach, and Om Beach are all connected by short auto-rickshaw rides or
    walkable paths in daylight. Most solo travellers get comfortable with the layout within a day.
    For after-dark trips between the beach and town, an auto-rickshaw is the simple, low-effort
    choice — they're easy to flag and inexpensive.
  </p>

  <h2>Meeting people without trying too hard</h2>
  <p>
    Hostels do most of the work here. A common area, a shared breakfast table, or a cafe that
    doubles as the hostel's living room means conversations start on their own. Guests at Aangan
    have described exactly this — a space where "you'll find a home here" and where hosts "put in
    effort to get everyone together," which is a low-pressure way to end up in a group for the beach
    trek or dinner without having to organize it yourself.
  </p>

  <h2>Is it safe for solo women travellers?</h2>
  <p>
    Gokarna is generally considered one of the more comfortable coastal towns in India for solo
    women travellers, particularly compared to more heavily nightlife-driven spots. Ordinary
    precautions still apply — stick to well-populated beaches after dark, let your hostel know your
    day plans, and pick accommodation with good reviews specifically from women travellers. One
    guest at Aangan wrote plainly: "If you are a solo female traveller, this is a perfect place for
    you to stay."
  </p>

  <h2>Picking where to stay</h2>
  <p>
    For solo travellers, the accommodation matters more than usual — it's your social anchor, not
    just a bed. Look for a hostel with a genuine common space (not just a dorm room), a location
    central enough to walk from, and reviews that specifically mention the vibe, not just the room
    quality.
  </p>

